-- title:
--   Twisted and Pi-translates carry even rigidifications
-- statement:
--   The statement is set up over the following data.
--
--   **Arithmetic and base data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ and a level $N \neq 0$, with $\bar r \neq r$, $r \nmid N$, $\bar r \nmid N$ and $N$ squarefree. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$, completeness of $\mathcal O$ for the $(\pi)$-adic topology, residue field of cardinality $r$, and the unramifiedness condition $(r) = (\pi)$; a characteristic-zero field $K_0$ which is the fraction field of $\mathcal O$. A characteristic-zero domain $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $\mathrm{Fr}$, subject to: $(\pi)$-adic completeness, maximality of the ideal generated by $\pi$, every element satisfying a monic $\mathcal O$-polynomial modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $\mathrm{Fr}(x) \equiv x^{r} \pmod \pi$ (`hFr`). A homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} \colon \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) which by `hvdet` is the $\pi$-adic valuation of the determinant: $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some $u \in \mathcal O^\times$.
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli spaces.** Rationals $a,b$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ indefinite and ramified exactly at $r$ and $\bar r$, and a maximal order $\Lambda$. A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point assignment $\mathrm{pt}$ which is a coarse moduli space for fake elliptic curves with $\Lambda$-action and level $N$ (`h𝒳`). An auxiliary level $n \geq 3$ prime to $r$, $\bar r$ and $N$, a fine moduli space $M$ over $\mathcal O$ for such curves with full level-$n$ structure (`hM`), a group $G$ acting on $M$ by level twists through $\rho$ and labels $\chi$ (`hρ`), and a forgetful morphism $p \colon M \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ (`hp`) which is $G$-invariant (`hρp`) and compatible with the point assignments (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell$ different from $r$ and $\bar r$, a coarse moduli space $\mathcal Y_\ell$ over $\mathcal O$ for curves with extra level-$\ell$ structure (`h𝒴`), with the two degeneracy morphisms $d_0,d_1 \colon \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ realising on points the forgetting of the extra level and the level-$\ell$ isogeny quotient (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`, `hd₀`, `hd₁`), and Atkin–Lehner morphisms $a_r, a_{\bar r} \colon \mathcal X \to \mathcal X$ over $\mathcal O$ realising the $r$- and $\bar r$-quotients on points (`harf`, `harbarf`, `har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$, a maximal order $\Lambda_1$, an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ contained in $\Lambda_1$, a finite-idelic unit $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ such that $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ is an Eichler order of level $Nr$, an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0 \colon \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$, and a place $v$ of $\mathbb Q$ above $r$. A subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]^\times$ which by `hΓt` consists exactly of the units integral at all places other than $v$ for $R_1$; elements $s_\ell$ and finite-idelic units $s^{f}_\ell$ indexed by the primes $\ell \neq r,\bar r$ satisfying the four clauses of `hs` (component of $s^f_\ell$ equal to $s_\ell \otimes 1$ away from $r$, equal to $1$ above $r$, the product of the diagonal idele of $\ell$ with $(s^f_\ell)^{-1}$ lying in the level Hecke set of $\Lambda_1$ and $R_1 \cap n_1R_1n_1^{-1}$ at $\ell$ when $\ell \mid N$ and in the prime Hecke set of that meet order otherwise, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s_\ell) = \ell$); the subgroups $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s_\ell\Gamma_t s_\ell^{-1}$; and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`).
--
--   **The distinguished curve over the residue field and its endomorphisms.** The hypothesis `hΛℤ` that all rational integers lie in $\Lambda$, and a map $\mathrm{coord}$ from $\Lambda$ to pairs of Witt vectors over $\mathbb F_{r^2}$ satisfying the order-coordinate axioms `hcoord` (additivity, normalisation at $1$, the twisted multiplication rule, injectivity, $r$-adic density, and the trace identity). A fake elliptic curve $A_0$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ over that residue ring (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ of dimension $2$ along the unit section of $A_0$, and the hypothesis `hA₀` that $\theta_0$ identifies the formal group of $A_0$ with $X_0$ compatibly with $\mathrm{coord}$. Families $e,e'$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $\Gamma_t$, with $e\gamma$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $\deg\gamma$, subject to: `hE1` (each pair $(e\gamma, e'\gamma)$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg\gamma}$ preserving the level-$N$ structure), `hE1mul` (multiplicativity up to multiplication by powers of $r$), `hE1sc` (rational scalars in $\Gamma_t$ act, up to powers of $r$, by the corresponding integer), `hE1'` (conversely, if $e\gamma$ becomes an integer multiplication after multiplication by a power of $r$, then $\gamma$ is a rational scalar), `hE2` (for every injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action and $X_0$-uniformiser endomorphisms into $M_2(K_0)$ there is a single $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $e\gamma$ is induced on $\theta_0$-coordinates by an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser whose matrix is $r^{k_\gamma}g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$), `hE3` (each full level-$n$ structure on $A_0$ yields a labelling $\Gamma_t \to \Lambda$ computing the action of $e\gamma$ on that structure, multiplicative modulo $n$ and matching rational scalars modulo $n$) and `hE4` (over every algebraically closed field over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$, every $r$-power-degree self-isogeny pair preserving the level on a curve pulled back from $A_0$ is, up to powers of $r$, induced by some $e\gamma$). An order $R_2 \leq R_1$ with $r$-power denominators clearing $R_1$ into $R_2$ and a family $\hat e$ of endomorphisms of $A_0$ indexed by $R_2$ over the base, subject to the five groups `hE5a`–`hE5e`: additivity on points, commutation with the $\Lambda$-action and preservation of the level; unitality, multiplicativity and agreement with integer multiplication; $\hat e(\bar x)\circ\hat e(x) = [\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$; agreement with $e\gamma$ for $x = r^{k}\gamma$ up to powers of $r$; and a simultaneous normalisation of $e$ and $\hat e$ in the formal-coordinate-and-matrix comparison of `hE2` with one common $g$.
--
--   **Formal moduli and the Drinfeld dictionary.** A ring homomorphism $\iota$ from the Witt vectors over $\mathbb F_{r^2}$ to $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$, a special formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ of height $4$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ (`hΦ`, `hΦ4`), a moduli package $MD$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`), and a map $\eta$ sending rigidified objects to points of $MD$ subject to the three clauses of `hη` (on admissible objects $\eta$ identifies exactly the isomorphic ones, $\eta$ is compatible with base change, and every point of $MD$ lies, locally for a finite cover of the base by principal opens, in the image of $\eta$ on admissible objects). An injective ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action and $\Phi$-uniformiser into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ with a single exponent $m$ (`hE₀`). A natural bijection $e^{D}$ (`eD`, `hnatD`, `hbijD`) from the functor of $G$-points of $MD$ on Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebras with $\pi$ nilpotent to the product of the functor $\psi \mapsto (O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to \!\!\cdot)$ and Deligne's functor $\Omega$ attached to $K_0, \pi$, compatible with the $O^{\mathrm{nr}}$-leg (`hfstD`), transporting the relation $\mathrm{IsActBy}$ by $g$ into the twisted action $\mathrm{IsTwistedAct}$ by $g$, that is, into the pair of conditions that the leg be the $-\mathrm{vdet}(g)$-th Frobenius twist and that the Deligne data be $g^{-1}$-pullbacks (`hGLD`), sending $\Pi$-translates to the pair consisting of the first Frobenius twist of the leg and the unchanged Deligne datum (`hPiD`), and with $\Pi$-translates always existing (`hPiexD`). A ring homomorphism $\kappa$ from $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$ to $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), and an isogeny $\beta_0$ of height $4n_0$ from $\Phi$ to the reduction of $X_0$ along $\kappa$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **The Atkin–Lehner datum over the residue field.** A fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ over $O^{\mathrm{nr}}/\pi$ together with morphisms $a_w, a_w'$ exhibiting it as the Atkin–Lehner $\bar r$-quotient of $A_0$ (`hALw`), an $r^{k_w}$-isogeny pair $b_w,b_w'$ back to $A_0$ preserving the level (`hBSw`, `hBSwlev`), and the hypothesis `hJOINTw` that for every injective $E_0$ as above a single $g$ simultaneously realises all $e\gamma$ by matrices $r^{k_\gamma}g\iota_0(\gamma)g^{-1}$ and realises the composite $a_w \!\cdot\! b_w$ by a matrix $r^{k_w}g\,\iota_0(\bar w)\,g^{-1}$.
--
--   **The comparison map.** A map $\Xi$ assigning to each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent, each $\psi \colon O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ and each pair consisting of a fake elliptic curve over $B$ and a rigidification of it relative to $(A_0,\psi)$ (a curve over $B/\pi$ pulled back from it, a curve over $B/\pi$ pulled back from $A_0$ along $\psi$, and an $r^{d}$-isogeny pair between them preserving the level) a $G$-point of $MD$ over $B$, subject to: `hΞleg` (for $B$ with no idempotents other than $0,1$ the leg of $\Xi$ is an integral Frobenius twist of $\psi$), `hΞnat` (naturality in $B$ for pullbacks of rigidified curves), `hΞiso` (invariance under isomorphisms of rigidified curves admitting comparison data on the two legs up to powers of $r$) and `hΞdef` (for connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent and a formal-module structure $(X,\theta)$ on the curve, there are $j \leq 1$ and an admissible rigidified object $t$ with $t.X = X$, transported from $\theta_0$ through $\kappa$ and $\beta_0$ with exponent $j$, such that $\Xi$ is the point with leg the $(-j)$-th Frobenius twist of $\psi$ and with $MD$-component $\eta(t)$). Finally a matrix $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ for which `heqΓ` states that a $\Gamma_t$-translation of a rigidification by $e\gamma$ is turned by $\Xi$ into an $\mathrm{IsActBy}$-relation for some central factor $r^{c}$ times $g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$, and `heqW` states the corresponding assertion for Atkin–Lehner $\bar r$-quotients, with $g_0\iota_0(\bar w)g_0^{-1}$ in place of $g_0\iota_0(\gamma)g_0^{-1}$, under the additional assumptions that $\bar r$ be invertible in $B$ and that the two rigidifications be linked by comparison data over the quotient map.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Two assertions hold. Throughout, $B$ is a Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent and whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, $\psi \colon O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$ is an $\mathcal O$-algebra map, $P$ is a Deligne datum over $B$, $E$ is a fake elliptic curve over $B$ with level $N$ and $\Lambda$-action, and $\varrho$ is a rigidification of $E$ relative to $A_0$ along the leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$; it is assumed that the rigidification is *even*, in the sense that the leg of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ is exactly $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$, and that $e^{D}$ of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ is the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted act of the pair $(\psi,P)$.
--
--   First assertion. For every further fake elliptic curve $E'$ over $B$, every rigidification $\varrho'$ of $E'$ along the same twisted leg, every unit $h$ of $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ and every $c \in \mathbb Z$ such that $\Xi(E',\varrho')$ is obtained from $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ by the relation $\mathrm{IsActBy}$ for the element $r^{c}\cdot g_0\,\iota_0(h)\,g_0^{-1}$ of $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$, and for every $\psi''$ and Deligne datum $P''$ over $B$ such that $(\psi'',P'')$ is the $\iota_0(h)$-twisted act of $(\psi,P)$, there exists a rigidification $\varrho''$ of the *same* curve $E'$ along the leg $\psi'' \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$ such that: the leg of $\Xi(E',\varrho'')$ equals $\psi'' \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$, so $\varrho''$ is again even; $e^{D}$ of $\Xi(E',\varrho'')$ is the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted act of $(\psi'',P'')$; and $\varrho''$ transports extra level structures exactly as $\varrho'$ does, namely for every prime $\ell \neq r$ invertible in $B$, every extra level-$\ell$ structure on $A_0$ (the binder for it reuses the identifier `K₀`, shadowing the fraction field) and all extra level-$\ell$ structures $C,C'$ on $E'$, if every point of the reduction of $E'$ whose image under $\varrho'$ lands in $C$ is carried by the isogeny of $\varrho'$ into the chosen structure on $A_0$, and likewise for $C'$ with $\varrho''$ in place of $\varrho'$, then $C$ and $C'$ cut out the same subfunctor: for every scheme $T$ over $\operatorname{Spec} B$ and every point $R$ of $E'$ over $T$, $R$ factors through $C$ if and only if it factors through $C'$.
--
--   Second assertion. For every fake elliptic curve $E'$ over $B$, every $\psi_1 \colon O^{\mathrm{nr}} \to B$, every rigidification $\varrho'$ of $E'$ along $\psi_1$, every $c \in \mathbb Z$ and every $G$-point $y$ of $MD$ over $B$ such that $y$ is a $\Pi$-translate of $\Xi(E,\varrho)$ and $\Xi(E',\varrho')$ is obtained from $y$ by the relation $\mathrm{IsActBy}$ for the central element $r^{c}$, there exists a rigidification $\varrho''$ of $E'$ along the leg $\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr} \circ \mathrm{Fr}^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}$ such that the leg of $\Xi(E',\varrho'')$ is that same leg, and $e^{D}$ of $\Xi(E',\varrho'')$ is the $g_0^{-1}$-twisted act of the pair $(\psi \circ \mathrm{Fr}, P)$. No clause on extra level structures is asserted in this second case.
--
--   This is the step in the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison that makes the dictionary between rigidified fake elliptic curves over $\pi$-nilpotent bases and points of the Drinfeld functor equivariant: translating a point by the image of a unit of the definite quaternion algebra, or by the Frobenius-type operator $\Pi$, can be realised by re-rigidifying the same curve so that the new rigidification is again even and has the prescribed $\Omega$-image, without disturbing the transported extra level structures away from $r$. It is used in the construction of the Čerednik–Drinfeld family over the fine moduli space.
